# unix-k1.Image / fw_payload.* -- build outputs of build-k1-payload.sh.
# Deliberately NOT tracked even though the maintainer needs a file to flash: it is
# regenerable in one command with the same pinned gcc (unlike user_elfs.h, which
# needs a cross toolchain that is not guaranteed present, and so IS tracked). A
# committed image that drifts from its source is worse than no image -- someone
# would flash a stale kernel and debug the wrong code on real hardware. The
# runbook tells the reader to run build-k1-payload.sh.
src/riscv/uts/unix-k1.Image
# unix-k3.Image + k3.dtb -- same reasoning, and it was COMMITTED BY ACCIDENT at
# 90f0ac680d, which is exactly the hazard the comment above forbids: a flashable
# kernel in git that the runbook tells the reader to rebuild. k3.dtb and
# k3.dtb.decompiled.dts are regenerated by build-k3-payload.sh on every run, so
# tracking them guarantees churn and invites flashing a stale pair.
src/riscv/uts/unix-k3.Image
src/riscv/uts/k3.dtb
src/riscv/uts/k3.dtb.decompiled.dts
src/riscv/uts/k1.dtb.decompiled.dts
src/riscv/uts/fw_payload.bin
src/riscv/uts/fw_payload.elf

# Build scratch.
wave12-work/
# Scratch copies of the RISC-V phase trees; their unique content is merged into
# the tracked src/riscv/rp*/ trees (verified: 0 sources missing).
_rp[0-9][0-9]/

# Photographs of hardware consoles. Console output belongs in the repo as TEXT
# (transcribed, greppable, diffable); a phone photo is a large binary that cannot
# be searched and may capture surroundings the maintainer did not intend to
# publish. Transcribe the numbers into a doc instead.
#
# Scoped to OUR directories on purpose: artifacts/sparc-xbuild/ contains vendored
# upstream source trees (libpng's pngbar.jpg, libuv's docs, texinfo test fixtures)
# whose own .jpg files are legitimately tracked. A blanket *.jpg would fight them.
docs/**/*.jpg
docs/**/*.jpeg
docs/**/*.heic
artifacts/install-media/**/*.jpg
artifacts/install-media/**/*.jpeg
artifacts/install-media/**/*.heic
artifacts/*.jpg
artifacts/*.jpeg
artifacts/*.heic
/*.jpg
/*.jpeg
/*.heic

# ⚠️ BUILD SCRATCH -- NEVER COMMIT. artifacts/sparc-xbuild alone held 1,187,182
# TRACKED files and 37 GB: extracted upstream sources with 24 copies of
# gengetopt-2.23.tar.xz, 8 of cairo-1.16.0.tar.xz, plus compiled test binaries.
# Nothing consumes it -- the only reference in the repo EXCLUDES it from integrity
# checks. It grew a 3.19 GiB pack and is why pushes to Codeberg started failing.
# The reusable part (build recipes, deduped failure lists, registry rows) is 192 KB
# and lives in artifacts/sparc-xbuild-recipes/.
artifacts/sparc-xbuild/
artifacts/*-xbuild/work*/
artifacts/*-xbuild/wave*/
artifacts/*-xbuild/debugbackfill*/
artifacts/ami-build/install/

